{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in with a bad headache?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started suddenly with flashing lights, just like my usual migraines. I took my sumatriptan but it didn’t help at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned it’s similar to your past migraines, which are usually on the right side. This one is on the left now—is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s unusual. But the throbbing, the light sensitivity—it feels like the same type. Just on the opposite side."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We checked your labs and a chest X-ray, which were normal. No fever or signs of infection. We gave you some medications in the ER—Toradol, Reglan, and Dilaudid. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still hurting. The pain’s a little less intense, but it’s not going away like it usually does."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history of stroke and migraines, we want to be cautious. We’re going to do a CT scan of your head to make sure there’s nothing new going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had a CTA recently—no aneurysms were found. But I understand if you need to double-check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2190-04-03 21:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that was outpatient. This is a non-contrast CT to rule out bleeding or stroke. We’ll get you scheduled right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. I have your CT head results. Good news—it shows no bleeding, no stroke, no new issues. Just some chronic changes from your past stroke, which are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why isn’t the migraine responding like it used to?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes migraines can become resistant, especially if they’re frequent. You mentioned your Botox injections help—when was your last one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A few months ago. My next appointment isn’t until next week. I was hoping to get it sooner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure your specialist knows you’re still struggling. In the meantime, we’re watching for any neurological changes. You mentioned earlier you had some trouble speaking and weakness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, last night—sudden aphasia and left arm weakness. But it went away by the time I got to CT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Neurology reviewed it. Given the transient nature and your history, they believe it’s part of your complex migraine, not a new stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve had those episodes before, always with bad migraines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring. Also, your abdominal pain—can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had nausea and cramping. No bowel movement or gas in over a day. I have a history of bowel obstructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a KUB—abdominal X-ray. It shows some dilated bowel loops. This suggests ileus, which is a temporary lack of movement in the intestines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it a blockage? I’ve had several small bowel obstructions before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray doesn’t show a complete blockage. It’s more consistent with ileus, which can happen after stress or illness. We’ve kept you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now and started IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My G-tube is supposed to help with decompression. Is it working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2190-04-04 04:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the tube is in place and functioning. We’re using it as needed. We’ll start you on clear liquids tomorrow if your symptoms improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the headache today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still there, but not as intense. The light sensitivity is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. And your belly—any nausea or pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still crampy, but I passed some gas last night. That’s a good sign, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very good. We’ll try advancing your diet to clear liquids today. If you tolerate that, we can move to soft foods tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. And what about the headache? Will it keep improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2190-04-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It seems to be resolving on its own. Since it’s not responding to usual meds, we’re relying on time and rest. Your Botox appointment is key for prevention moving forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You’re looking more comfortable. Headache still present?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a dull ache now. I didn’t need any pain meds overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. And your abdomen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I had a small bowel movement this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great news. Means your ileus is resolving. We’ll keep you on soft diet and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. One thing—my G-tube stitching came loose yesterday. The nurse said it was replaced."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2190-04-06 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was re-secured. The site has mild redness, but no signs of infection. Keep it clean and dry at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. How are you feeling overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really good. Headache is almost gone. Belly feels normal. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. Your labs are stable. Blood cultures were negative—no infection. We’ll send a summary to your PCP and neurologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I get my iron infusion? I missed one while I was here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s scheduled for next week. We’ll coordinate with your infusion center."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my Botox appointment—is it still on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ve flagged that you’re still having migraines. They may move it up or adjust your plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been relying on that for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We also checked your thyroid—TSH is a bit high, but your free T4 is normal. Your endocrinologist should follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have hypothyroidism. I take levothyroxine—should I adjust the dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2190-04-07 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not without checking with your doctor. We’ll note it for your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re discharging you today. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If the headache returns severely, or you have weakness, trouble speaking, or belly pain with vomiting, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my meds—same as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your home medications are continued. Take the sumatriptan only as needed, and avoid overuse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure your specialists have all the details. Take care, and follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you hopefully not too soon!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hopefully not! But we’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—my G-tube site is a little red. Should I use any cream?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just keep it clean with soap and water. If it gets more red, swollen, or starts draining, call your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ll watch it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. The discharge nurse will go over instructions and get you on your way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Take care!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2190-04-08 11:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll be there."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2190-04-03 21:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2190-04-08 17:01:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of complex migraines, sclerosing mesenteritis, and gastrostomy status was admitted for a severe migraine with aura, which was resistant to standard treatment. Imaging showed no acute intracranial pathology, and transient aphasia and left-sided weakness were attributed to her migraine pattern. During admission, she was found to have an ileus, likely related to her history of bowel dysmotility, which was managed conservatively with NPO status, IV fluids, and symptom control. Her headache and ileus gradually improved over several days. The G-tube site required recannulation due to loosened sutures. She was discharged home in stable condition with plans to follow up with her neurologist for Botox injection and to resume her missed iron infusion, with instructions to monitor for recurrence of neurological or abdominal symptoms.",
    "problems": [
      "Migraine with aura, intractable, without status migrainosus",
      "Ileus, unspecified",
      "Encounter for attention to gastrostomy",
      "Aphasia",
      "Weakness",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Iron deficiency anemia secondary to blood loss (chronic)",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Major depressive disorder, recurrent, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
